## Install, and roll back

Follow the [README](https://github.com/joegiralt/chimera-releases#readme): it has the DFU steps to install, and the steps to go back to the stock firmware. Flash the firmware area only (`0x08020000`); never the bootloader, never the option bytes. Chimera only reads and writes `/CHIMERA/` on the SD card and never touches your stock files.

## Known issues

See [KNOWN-ISSUES.md](https://github.com/joegiralt/chimera-releases/blob/main/KNOWN-ISSUES.md).

## Boards

Chimera reads the main board at boot and shows it on SETTINGS › SYSTEM › ABOUT (the CHIP cell). The LQFP176 board is tested. The newer "1.6 - 100" board (LQFP100) is supported but not yet tried on hardware: if you have one, please report how it goes.

## Reporting bugs

[Open a bug report](https://github.com/joegiralt/chimera-releases/issues/new/choose). Give the firmware version (shown at boot), what you did, and what you heard or saw; a short recording or photo helps.

